course: dictionary
lesson: 9480
title: Stay and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stay is a small word with many meanings, so the context tells you which one is meant. Ask yourself: is something staying in one place, staying the same, or is it a time spent somewhere? «A dog that growls, shows its teeth or goes stiff is warning you to stay away.» Here stay away means keep your distance, because the dog is warning you.
explain: «If you lose your place, staying calm and carrying on usually works.» Here stay means keep being calm, not stay in one place. Try a swap: keeping calm and carrying on usually works. It still makes sense, so keep is a good match for stay in this sentence.
explain: Stay can also be a noun. «A short stay in hospital» is a time spent somewhere. When you meet stay, check which job it does in the sentence: is it an action (a verb) or a thing or time (a noun)?
fact: Stay means to remain in the same place, as in stay at home.
fact: Stay means to keep being the same, as in stay calm or stay dry.
fact: A stay is a time spent somewhere, as in «a short stay in hospital».
fact: «Stay put» means do not move, and «stay up» means do not go to bed.
fact: «Stay!» is a command to a dog, meaning do not move.
exercise: «A dog that growls, shows its teeth or goes stiff is warning you to stay away.» What does stay away mean? | Run round in circles | Come closer and say hello | *Keep your distance | Sit down and wait for a treat
exercise: «If you lose your place, staying calm and carrying on usually works.» What does staying calm mean here? | Moving quickly to a new place | Shouting for help | Going to sleep early | *Keeping calm and not panicking
exercise: «A short stay in hospital» is a time spent somewhere. What kind of word is stay here? | A question word | An adjective | *A noun | A verb
test: «Chloe stays polite but stops sharing secrets.» What does stays mean here? | *Keeps being | Sings loudly to | Moves away from | Goes to bed at
test: «Stay put until your teacher comes back.» What does stay put mean? | Run to the door | Stay up late | Go home early | *Do not move
exam: «Mia asked, "Can I stay over at your house tonight?"» What does stay over mean? | Leave early for home | Wait for the bus | Stay in and not go out | *Sleep at a friend's house
